   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I see that when we use WLSMV, the observed and model-implied covariances are actually correlations</div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Yes, with categorical indicators, the model is fit to their estimated polychoric correlation matrix (which is treated as the &quot;observed&quot; covariance matrix that the model tries to reproduce).</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
